{"name":"Clay Court","hex":"#a9765d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clay court","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of claycourt."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clay_court"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clay court","blocks":[{"text":"A clay court is one of the types of tennis court on which the sport of tennis is played. Clay courts are built on a foundation of crushed stone, particularly limestone, shale, and other aggregate, with a thin layer of fine clay particles on top. Clay courts are more common in Continental Europe and Latin America than in North America, Asia-Pacific, or Britain. The only Grand Slam tournament that uses clay courts is the French Open."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/ND_DN_2006FO.jpg/330px-ND_DN_2006FO.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clay_court","wikidata":"Q198718"},{"title":"Clay","blocks":[{"text":"Clay is a type of fine-grained natural soil material containing clay minerals. Most pure clay minerals are white or light-coloured, but natural clays show a variety of colours from impurities, such as a reddish or brownish colour from small amounts of iron oxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg/330px-Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clay","wikidata":"Q42302"},{"title":"Court","blocks":[{"text":"A court is an institution, often a government entity, with the authority to adjudicate legal disputes between parties and administer justice in civil, criminal, and administrative matters in accordance with the rule of law."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Microcosm_of_London_Plate_058_-_Old_Bailey_edited.jpg/330px-Microcosm_of_London_Plate_058_-_Old_Bailey_edited.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Court","wikidata":"Q41487"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Munitions_Production_on_the_Home_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q30557.jpg/500px-Munitions_Production_on_the_Home_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q30557.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Munitions_Production_on_the_Home_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q30557.jpg/1280px-Munitions_Production_on_the_Home_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q30557.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Munitions_Production_on_the_Home_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q30557.jpg/500px-Munitions_Production_on_the_Home_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q30557.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A clay court being rolled at Gretna Green, Scotland, in the 1910s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMunitions_Production_on_the_Home_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q30557.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tennis_Courts%2C_Kirkton_Park_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1306458.jpg/500px-Tennis_Courts%2C_Kirkton_Park_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1306458.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tennis_Courts%2C_Kirkton_Park_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1306458.jpg/500px-Tennis_Courts%2C_Kirkton_Park_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1306458.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A shale or \"blaes\" court, as seen here in Scotland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATennis_Courts%2C_Kirkton_Park_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1306458.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Sanchai_and_Sonchat_Ratiw